    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Many (most?) decimal values are not exactly representable in a fixed-precision binary floating point representation. So I suspect a discrepancy between the algorithms used for parsing and converting a string decimal value to a binary floating point value. Notice that the cuDF discrepancy is at a precision range way beyond the precision of the values specified in the CSV. Pandas has multiple conversion options. I'm betting that you may be able to match the cuDF results using one of Pandas other options. http://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/io.html#specifying-method-for-floating-point-conversion I read that the default may sacrifice some accuracy for speed.",
